1
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:02,750
Dammit!

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:05,710
Everyone on the team... 
knows how you must feel.

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,460
So I think...

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:13,500
...that's exactly why Nanao decided
to ask you that question... in front of all of us.

5
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:17,000
And in that moment, you answered clearly.

6
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:20,630
It psyched me up. Seeing your bravery.

7
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:26,540
Y-yeah.

8
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:58,000
Ahiru no Sora

9
00:01:57,750 --> 00:01:59,880
Nice, Chucky!

10
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:01,880
VOW

11
00:02:00,380 --> 00:02:07,170
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense!

12
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,330
Shit, they just won't let up.

13
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,830
Only 3 more minutes...

14
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,330
We're not losing the lead now!
Keep your heads in the game!

15
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,420
The first match of the day
is turning out to be a real spectacle.

16
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:23,540
If memory serves, neither of these schools
even entered the tourney last year.

17
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:28,040
What a shame! They've both 
got such amazing players.

18
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:30,090
I hope this is a sign 
that more high schoolers

19
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:32,290
are taking an interest in 
the game of basketball.

20
00:02:35,330 --> 00:02:36,500
He's boxing me out!

21
00:02:40,330 --> 00:02:43,420
Koji and I were the only 
members in our freshmen year.

22
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:46,420
Playing in a game like this was a pipe dream.

23
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,540
Basketball
Team

24
00:02:47,710 --> 00:02:50,920
The year after that, we still 
couldn't get up to 5 members.

25
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:51,380
Basketball
Team

26
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:56,540
And now our first go at the inter-high tourney...
is also our last!

27
00:02:56,830 --> 00:02:58,000
Did he foul...?

28
00:02:58,790 --> 00:03:00,460
No, they're not calling it.

29
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:01,790
I let him get by!

30
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:05,880
We can't afford to waste all our stamina
in this very first game!

31
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:07,330
Not on my watch!

32
00:03:12,210 --> 00:03:12,960
Loose ball!

33
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,000
A three-pointer!

34
00:03:18,790 --> 00:03:19,750
Rebound!

35
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:21,170
It went in!

36
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:23,630
Now we're ahead by 4!

37
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,750
Simply wonderful, Roku!

38
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:26,580
Thanks.

39
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:29,250
Okay, just a bit more!

40
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:31,210
Let's go into the second 
half with a solid lead!

41
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,330
Right!

42
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,830
We WILL win this!

43
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:44,830
Defense! Defense! Defense! Defense!

44
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,210
The first half is just about to end.

45
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,830
We have to avoid letting them
get a huge lead here at the very least.

46
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,000
That means no screw ups.

47
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:49,210
We have to keep up with them no matter what!

48
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:52,040
Until Chiaki comes back into the game!

49
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:54,830
The qualities that a good 
point guard needs most?

50
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:59,000
That's simple, a manly attitude 
and chiseled good looks.

51
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,630
But Chiaki... you don't have any of that.

52
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:07,960
If I have to be real,
then an eye for opportunity is essential.

53
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,250
Particularly when it comes to hot babes.

54
00:04:11,290 --> 00:04:14,250
You always fail 'cuz you try
to memorize them one-by-one.

55
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:18,710
You'll never be a good point guard
unless you learn to look at the bigger picture.

56
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:23,960
Channel your five senses.
Your whole team is aiming for the basket.

57
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Nice pass!

58
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:36,210
That pass got them into a good spot!

59
00:04:36,210 --> 00:04:37,750
That guy has some smooth moves!

60
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:41,920
It's a hook! Get on the 
side with the ball, Yukio!

61
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:45,540
LIGHT

62
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,420
I guess he really does know his shit.

63
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:48,750
GREASED
LIGHTNING

64
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:58,460
Pretty good. Is this how 
Kuzu High always plays?

65
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:01,540
Dunno. This is the first year 
they've ever participated.

66
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,380
It's a good thing we came to check them out.

67
00:05:03,750 --> 00:05:05,130
Nice assist!

68
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:07,630
Right back at you. Great pass, Kurumatani.

69
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:09,880
You missed me making a cut 
for the basket three times.

70
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,250
You gotta pay more attention.

71
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:13,670
Sorry.

72
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,870
He sure likes to gets on everybody's case,

73
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:18,050
but I have to admit he plays the game well.

74
00:05:20,330 --> 00:05:24,250
But honestly, the more I look at it,
the weirder his hair gets.

75
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:26,290
Huh? Did you say something?

76
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,580
That's our freshmen trio.

77
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:30,580
They're pretty damn impressive.

78
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:33,080
All right! Time to totally shut them down!

79
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,420
Bring the pain!

80
00:05:42,210 --> 00:05:43,960
I screwed up...!

81
00:05:44,630 --> 00:05:46,380
Holding! White #6!

82
00:05:50,130 --> 00:05:52,790
That damn attention whore. 
I'll make him pay for this.

83
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:58,500
He made me look like a complete fool
in front of everyone.

84
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:02,790
And the worst part is...

85
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,710
...Nao saw every second of it!

86
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,920
He missed the second one!

87
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:11,630
Whoa! Nice rebound!

88
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:14,750
We're pretty much invincible under the basket
now thanks to Momoharu and Mokichi!

89
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,960
I think we're really starting 
to turn this around!

90
00:06:17,330 --> 00:06:20,170
We can probably hold our own
for a while even without Chiaki!

91
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,420
Don't ya think so, Nao?

92
00:06:21,420 --> 00:06:23,630
Huh? Oh, I suppose so.

93
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:25,880
Sweet! I'm getting psyched up now!

94
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:28,790
Damn. It won't go in!

95
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:30,710
Counter!

96
00:06:36,130 --> 00:06:37,790
That one's gonna hurt bad.

97
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:40,080
Right after things started going their way.

98
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,290
Hey, Mokichi.

99
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,420
You okay?

100
00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:49,630
Oh, yeah. I'm fine.

101
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,040
I see... I hadn't noticed until now,

102
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,680
but since they have to run between 
the very ends of the court

103
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:58,000
the center has the most strenuous job of all.

104
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,500
I've gotta switch up the 
rhythm of our offense,

105
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,670
and spread out the burden 
among us more equally.

106
00:07:03,310 --> 00:07:05,770
We've been playing almost exclusively
in the post for a while now.

107
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,790
Is that little idiot trying to kill me?!

108
00:07:23,830 --> 00:07:26,670
Holy cow! Did you see that pass just now?

109
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:28,080
He chucked it from behind 
the half court line!

110
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:31,040
Our resident shorty is 
starting to find his groove!

111
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,420
Ain't that right, Chiaki?

112
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,080
Huh?

113
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,210
Chiaki...?

114
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:41,670
That's the end of the first half!

115
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:45,670
It's down to a 2 point game.
Shinjo worked hard to defend their lead.

116
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:47,830
That last pass was really incredible though.

117
00:07:47,830 --> 00:07:51,630
Man, this game is super high 
level. Both teams are good.

118
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,440
It seems they were evenly matched
for the entire first half.

119
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,210
Well, I'm not surprised.

120
00:07:56,630 --> 00:07:58,720
The second half will test 
more than skill, the team

121
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,580
with the better stamina and 
concentration will cinch it.

122
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:05,000
This is where they're going to have
to set themselves apart.

123
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:09,920
Alrighty then. It's about time for us
to start warming up. Let's move!

124
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,000
Roger that.

125
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:17,040
He's nothing at all like 
when we played before.

126
00:08:17,290 --> 00:08:19,250
I can tell that he really 
practiced his ass off.

127
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,630
I'm looking forward to our rematch.

128
00:08:24,330 --> 00:08:26,670
Huh? Where'd Chiaki and Nanao go?

129
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:31,920
Yeah, about that... Chiaki just up and vanished
a couple of minutes ago.

130
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,880
So Nao had to leave to go and check on him.

131
00:08:35,250 --> 00:08:37,290
Where do you think he got off to?

132
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,290
Dunno.

133
00:08:38,290 --> 00:08:39,830
Must be taking a shit or something.

134
00:08:40,210 --> 00:08:42,000
I'm sure he'll be back soon.

135
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:45,130
We have more important things 
to focus on right now.

136
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:49,540
Everybody needs to rest up and recover
what stamina they can before the second half starts.

137
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:54,670
Goddammit... I totally spaced
on how rotten his attitude can get!

138
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:58,380
The hell are you doing, man?!
We're still in the middle of a game!

139
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:00,710
I mean, there's no point if we can't win.

140
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:04,540
I don't wanna keep playing 
when we look so uncool.

141
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:08,380
Don't tell me... that bastard did it again?!

142
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:11,670
What's the matter, Captain?
You look like you're gonna puke.

143
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,460
HURRY!

144
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:16,880
Get the lead out, Kato! We gotta speed it up!

145
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:20,080
I'm telling you, we don't have to rush
because it's only halftime!

146
00:09:18,130 --> 00:09:19,130
Hurry!

147
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:25,460
But I... want to spend as much time
in Nao's presence as possible.

148
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:26,380
Hold up a sec!

149
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,170
Wait, don't pull!

150
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:29,420
WHAT THE HELL, MAN?!

151
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:30,830
Look... over there.

152
00:09:30,830 --> 00:09:31,880
Huh?

153
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:42,670
That's gotta be somebody else.
There's no way he'd be here.

154
00:09:42,670 --> 00:09:44,960
But he's wearing the 
uniform and everything...

155
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:46,290
He's coming this way!

156
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:50,960
Why is he chasing us?!

157
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:53,290
And why the hell is the 
cashier following after him?!

158
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:56,750
Premium Popsicle Soda Flavor
Total: 5 Items
Yen

159
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,750
Th-that'll be 324 yen, please.

160
00:09:57,130 --> 00:10:00,920
Don't eat popsicles you that can't pay for, dammit!
Especially not FIVE of them!

161
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:01,880
And this, too.

162
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,210
Just put the magazine back!

163
00:10:04,330 --> 00:10:06,210
3 fouls in the first half?

164
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:08,750
Damn, that's gotta be rough.

165
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:11,830
I actually got 4 in our game today,
so it's a big problem for me, too.

166
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:14,560
I don't care about the peanut gallery,

167
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:17,590
but Nao is the one person I  
never want to see me as uncool.

168
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:18,750
Huh?

169
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,330
MIYUKI OVERPASS

170
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,580
Did Nao actually say that to you?

171
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:23,830
That you were "uncool"?

172
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:31,460
I figured. She's not the type
to look down on people like that.

173
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,630
Back when I first started 
and absolutely sucked,

174
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:39,330
and even when our team got wrecked
by stronger schools...

175
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:43,380
...Nao would always cheer 
me on with a big smile.

176
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:49,960
To her, I always looked cool on the court.
She's never said anything different.

177
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:56,210
So don't you dare... 
disrespect Nao like that!

178
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:00,330
Taro...

179
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:03,750
I guess this Suzuki dude is a 
pretty decent guy after all.

180
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:04,500
Huh?

181
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:06,420
Just who the hell is Suzuki?!

182
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:08,330
Huh? Wasn't that your name?

183
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,460
In any case, you should 
really get back there.

184
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:13,750
It's not unheard of to get a 
technical foul for ditching.

185
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:14,960
Seriously?

186
00:11:15,210 --> 00:11:17,460
Not to mention, any team 
will struggle to play

187
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:20,150
without their point guard, 
three fouls or not.

188
00:11:22,290 --> 00:11:25,170
We can probably hold our own for a while
even without Chiaki!

189
00:11:25,170 --> 00:11:27,330
Huh? Oh, I suppose so.

190
00:11:27,330 --> 00:11:29,710
No... I'm not...

191
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:32,830
Chiaki!

192
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,420
Nao...

193
00:11:39,330 --> 00:11:42,210
Hey, Nao! You came all this way to meet me?

194
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:44,960
My angel!

195
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,710
Huh? What are you doing out here Taro?!

196
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,750
Hey, Nao, you've got some 
blood on your knee...

197
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,170
Oh... I tripped and fell a minute ago.

198
00:11:53,330 --> 00:11:56,170
I've been worried about you.
What on Earth made you disappear like that?

199
00:11:56,330 --> 00:11:59,420
She came... all the way out here to find me?

200
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:02,920
She ran herself ragged just for me?

201
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:07,540
What a relief. I had no idea
what I was going to do if I couldn't find you.

202
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:12,040
Shit. I look... drastically uncool right now.

203
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:15,000
Now listen here!
Whenever you get benched from now on...

204
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:20,000
I'm begging you, Nao. Just 
please don't look at me...

205
00:12:20,630 --> 00:12:21,710
Here, take this!

206
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:25,940
Use it to wipe off your sweat.

207
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:28,850
Make sure you keep your 
body from getting too cold.

208
00:12:29,210 --> 00:12:34,000
Everybody worked real hard out there
to make sure you wouldn't come back to a big mess.

209
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:36,330
So be sure to show your 
appreciation later, okay?

210
00:12:36,710 --> 00:12:38,960
Oh, I get it...

211
00:12:40,170 --> 00:12:45,420
Nao's already seen it,
she's always watched us struggle to improve...

212
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:50,960
Okay! I need to get back right away
to have a meeting with the others.

213
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:54,210
But I want you to walk back slowly
so you don't get tired, Chiaki.

214
00:12:54,210 --> 00:12:56,000
There's still plenty of time left!

215
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,750
It's just like seaweed head said...

216
00:13:03,170 --> 00:13:04,330
All right!

217
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:06,790
We gotta get going too, Kato!

218
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:07,880
Wait!

219
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,330
What? What do you want this time?

220
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:14,290
You're going down, seaweed head.
I'll become the most important person to Nao.

221
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:16,420
Huh?! What the hell?!

222
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:20,710
In other words, I'm going to become
the best basketball player in Japan.

223
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:21,880
Huh?

224
00:13:22,330 --> 00:13:25,960
I will... never lose to anyone!

225
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:38,290
Juri? What's up with this text?
How'd she get her hands on a phone?

226
00:13:38,290 --> 00:13:41,290
bought a celly
r u playing now?

227
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:41,290
Jeez, she ain't even using full sentences.

228
